--TEST--
`foreach` refuses every subject `rule:iteration/foreach-subjects`'s closed list does not name, a `void` call among them, and defers only a `mixed` — `rule:iteration/foreach-subjects`, `rule:types/conversion`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:iteration/foreach-subjects`'s list is closed — an `array<T>`, an `Iterable<T>` or an
// `Iterator<T>` — so a subject naming none of them has no elements to yield
// and is refused where it is written rather than answered below. This sweeps
// one spelling per shape, in source order, so a shape that stopped refusing
// shows up as a missing line rather than as a plausible empty loop.
//
// A call that returns `void` is the shape this case was written for, and it
// is one step earlier than the rest: the others have a type that answers the
// question, while a `void` call has no value for the question to be about.
// It is `E0443` and not the condition's `E0719` or the operand's `E0718`,
// because a subject is neither — `nvs_types::expr::iteration`'s
// `report_not_iterable` is that refusal's one home.
class Effect {
    public static function run(): void {}
}
class Plain {
    public int $n = 1;
}

int $i = 7;
string $s = "ab";
bool $b = true;
?string $optional = null;
Plain $o = new Plain();

foreach (Effect::run() as int $a) { echo $a; }
foreach ($i as int $c) { echo $c; }
foreach ($s as string $d) { echo $d; }
foreach ($b as bool $e) { echo $e; }
// A union naming no iterable type is judged as the union, not as its widest
// member: the nullable half is exactly what a `foreach` cannot walk.
foreach ($optional as string $f) { echo $f; }
// An object is refused for naming neither interface — `rule:iteration/concrete-generic-implements` makes
// `Iterable`/`Iterator` the only two, so there is no other way in.
foreach ($o as int $g) { echo $g; }

// The one subject that is *not* refused, and is deliberately last: `mixed` is
// `rule:types/conversion`'s one unchecked position, so it defers whether there is an
// array behind the handle at all rather than answering now. A line that
// started refusing it would add a seventh error below.
mixed $m = [1, 2];
foreach ($m as int $h) { echo $h; }
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0443]: `foreach` cannot iterate a `void`
%A
error[E0443]: `foreach` cannot iterate a `int`
%A
error[E0443]: `foreach` cannot iterate a `string`
%A
error[E0443]: `foreach` cannot iterate a `bool`
%A
error[E0443]: `foreach` cannot iterate a `string|null`
%A
error[E0443]: `foreach` cannot iterate a `Plain`
%A
error: aborting due to 6 errors
